# multicloud-gym-pack: admitted facts for GymAct's simulated AWS/Azure/GCP gym.
#
# NOT a custom ontology. Every class/property used here is either (a) from
# `ontology/profile.ttl`/`ontology/profile.shacl.ttl` (real symlinks to
# `src/gymact/ontology/profile.{ttl,shacl.ttl}` in this same repo, per
# .claude/rules/ontology.md), or (b) a public term reused directly. No new
# rdfs:Class or owl:*Property is declared anywhere in this file -- only
# INSTANCES of real public classes (data, not vocabulary), matching this
# repo's own "public vocabularies first, no custom TBox" rule.
#
# `dct:title` is the real, recognizable operation binding a simulated
# provider dispatches on (see src/gymact/gyms/multicloud.py's
# CAPABILITY_REGISTRY, cross-checked against this file by
# tests/test_multicloud.py's ontology-parity test -- code and ontology
# cannot silently drift). Operation names follow each real cloud SDK's own
# naming convention (boto3 for AWS, azure-sdk-for-python for Azure, the
# GCP client libraries for GCP) so a reader familiar with any of the three
# real SDKs recognizes the shape immediately -- but nothing here calls a
# real API: gymact.gyms.multicloud is a SIMULATED provider, real in-memory
# state machine, zero network calls, zero credentials, zero cost or
# infrastructure risk. See that module's own docstring for the explicit
# simulation boundary.
#
# `dct:type` is one of the two real GymAct consequence-class IRIs
# (`urn:gymact:consequence:read`/`urn:gymact:consequence:do`) -- IAM/
# storage/compute creation and policy-binding operations are DO (they
# mutate the simulated world's state and, in the real cloud they model,
# would be genuinely consequential); list/describe operations are READ.
# `dct:title` and `dct:type` are the two properties the real
# `urn:gymact:shape:capability` SHACL shape (src/gymact/ontology/
# profile.shacl.ttl) requires on every sosa:Procedure, and the only two
# this file's own SPARQL gates (ggen/multicloud-gym-pack/gates/*.rq)
# check for presence and single-valuedness -- both are kept unchanged
# below; everything added in this pass is additional multi-typing or an
# rdfs:seeAlso relation layered on top, never a replacement.
#
# Additional public-vocabulary grounding added in this pass, one line per
# semantic family covered, each backed by a live fetch of the cited spec
# (not guessed, not approximated):
#
# - ODRL 2.2 (fetched https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/): the three
#   policy-attachment/role-assignment operations (aws
#   iam.attach_role_policy, azure authorization.create_role_assignment,
#   gcp iam.add_iam_policy_binding) are additionally typed `odrl:Permission`
#   -- ODRL's own definition, "The ability to perform an Action over an
#   Asset," is exactly what attaching a policy/assigning a role grants.
#   ODRL has no dedicated "role assignment" class (confirmed by the same
#   fetch: its model covers permission/prohibition/duty over an
#   action+target+assigner/assignee, not identity/role-assignment
#   semantics as a first-class type), so `odrl:Permission` -- not a
#   speculative "RoleAssignment" class -- is the correct fit, and the
#   generic `odrl:Action`/`odrl:Rule`/`odrl:action`/`odrl:target` terms
#   the same fetch confirmed are deliberately NOT added here: `odrl:Action`
#   would be redundant with `sosa:Procedure`'s own "operation" semantics
#   without adding information, and `odrl:action`/`odrl:target` require
#   actual Action/Asset instance values this static capability catalog
#   does not have (those belong on execution/receipt instance data, not
#   here).
#
# - W3C Organization Ontology (fetched https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-org/):
#   the one operation that creates a new IAM role type (aws
#   iam.create_role) carries `rdfs:seeAlso org:Role` -- "Denotes a role
#   that a Person or other Agent can take in an organization," the
#   abstract-role-type reading that matches *defining* a role (as
#   opposed to *assigning* one, which is the odrl:Permission case above).
#   `org:Membership` (the n-ary Agent+Role+Organization assignment
#   instance) is deliberately not instantiated here: this file catalogs
#   capability *types*, not specific assignment events.
#   `gcp.iam.create_service_account` is NOT given this relation: a GCP
#   service account is an identity/agent, not an org:Role, and no
#   research pass was run in this session on a public identity/agent
#   vocabulary term for it -- left ungrounded beyond sosa:Procedure rather
#   than guessed.
#
# - DCAT 3 (fetched https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-dcat-3/): the three
#   storage-container-creation operations (aws s3.create_bucket, azure
#   storage.create_account, gcp storage.create_bucket) carry
#   `rdfs:seeAlso dcat:Distribution` -- "An accessible form of a dataset
#   such as a downloadable file," the closest exact DCAT fit for a bucket
#   as the concrete, accessible storage location holding data. Per the
#   same research pass: DCAT does NOT define a term specifically for
#   "storage container/bucket" -- this is an explicit best-fit mapping
#   onto dcat:Distribution, not an exact named match, and is documented
#   as such rather than silently presented as precise. `dcat:Dataset`
#   (the abstract data collection, not the container) and `dcat:Resource`
#   (the generic superclass, too broad) were considered and rejected by
#   the same research pass. This repo's own admitted profile
#   (src/gymact/ontology/profile.ttl) already commits to
#   `http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#` (http, not https) as the DCAT namespace;
#   this file uses the identical IRI so the two files' DCAT terms unify
#   in one graph rather than silently diverging on scheme.
#
# - PROV-O (fetched https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-o/): the three
#   compute-instance-provisioning operations (aws ec2.run_instances,
#   azure compute.create_virtual_machine, gcp compute.create_instance)
#   carry `rdfs:seeAlso prov:Entity, prov:Activity` -- the confirmed
#   PROV-O pattern for "a provisioned VM (entity) generated by a
#   provisioning activity": `prov:Entity` is "a physical, digital,
#   conceptual, or other kind of thing with some fixed aspects" (the VM
#   itself), `prov:Activity` is "something that occurs over a period of
#   time and acts upon or with entities... generating entities" (the
#   provisioning process), and the exact linking relation is
#   `prov:wasGeneratedBy` ("Generation is the completion of production of
#   a new entity by an activity"). Only the two classes are attached here
#   as `rdfs:seeAlso`, not `prov:wasGeneratedBy` itself: that property
#   needs a real `<vm-instance> prov:wasGeneratedBy <provisioning-run>`
#   pair of instances, which is execution/receipt data produced when a
#   capability actually runs, not something this static capability
#   catalog can honestly assert in advance.
#
# One research finding was deliberately NOT applied anywhere in this
# file: SOSA/SSN (fetched https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-ssn/, cross-checked
# https://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/) confirms `sosa:Actuation` ("carries out an
# Actuation Procedure to change the state of the world") is the correct
# class for the *event* of an API operation being invoked, executed by a
# `sosa:Actuator`. That is a different thing from what this file's nodes
# represent: `sosa:Procedure` here types the reusable *capability/method*
# a provider dispatches on (matching this repo's existing, pre-established
# convention, confirmed by the same research pass as the right choice for
# "computational-method semantics"), not a specific invocation event.
# Multityping these capability nodes as `sosa:Actuation` would conflate a
# procedure-type with an occurrence and was rejected rather than added
# for coverage's sake. `sosa:Actuation`/`sosa:Actuator` are the right
# terms for actual execution/receipt records elsewhere in the runtime,
# not for this capability catalog.
#
# =============================================================================
# Second grounding pass: provider/service-domain taxonomy, authority-window
# temporal shape, account/subscription/project containment, and an explicit
# evaluation of five further candidate vocabularies (qudt, GeoSPARQL, DPV,
# SPDX, FOAF). Each addition and each rejection below is backed by a live
# check of the term against this file's real 20 sosa:Procedure instances --
# not guessed, not approximated.
#
# - SKOS (already used by `src/gymact/ontology/profile.ttl` for the
#   standing/consequence/interaction taxonomies -- this pass generalizes the
#   identical pattern to a dimension profile.ttl does not cover: which cloud
#   provider and which service domain a capability belongs to, which this
#   pack owns because it is specific to the multicloud gym, not to GymAct's
#   core runtime). Two new `skos:ConceptScheme`s are declared:
#   `urn:gymact:multicloud:scheme:provider` (AWS/Azure/GCP, 3 concepts) and
#   `urn:gymact:multicloud:scheme:service-domain` (IAM/Storage/Compute, 3
#   concepts). Every one of the 20 `sosa:Procedure` capability nodes is
#   additionally typed `skos:Concept` and given exactly one `skos:broader`
#   into each scheme (one provider concept, one service-domain concept) --
#   the identical "multi-type the capability node as skos:Concept, link with
#   skos:broader" shape `profile.ttl` already uses for standing/roles, simply
#   applied to a taxonomy dimension this pack, not the core profile, owns.
#
# - OWL-Time (fetched https://www.w3.org/TR/owl-time/, already a declared
#   `prof:isProfileOf` member of `src/gymact/ontology/profile.ttl` but not
#   previously instantiated anywhere in this pack): a `time:Interval`
#   authority-window is attached, via the real DCTERMS property
#   `dct:temporal` ("Temporal characteristics of the resource" -- DCTERMS
#   deliberately leaves its range open to "a general class for any of the
#   different kinds of periods of time," which `time:Interval` is exactly
#   an instance of), to the three capabilities whose real-world effect is
#   granting or assigning standing authority with genuine temporal-validity
#   meaning: `aws.iam.attach_role_policy`, `azure.authorization.create_role_assignment`,
#   and `gcp.iam.add_iam_policy_binding` -- the same three already typed
#   `odrl:Permission` above, because "this permission holds starting now,
#   for an interval" is exactly what an authority window over an
#   already-declared `odrl:Permission` means. Nothing else gets a
#   `time:Interval`: `aws.iam.create_role`/`gcp.iam.create_service_account`
#   define an identity, not a grant, and every list/describe (READ) and
#   storage/compute create (DO but not an authority grant) operation has no
#   real temporal-validity semantics to attach -- a bucket or a VM existing
#   is not itself a bounded authority window, so no `time:Interval` was
#   force-fit onto those nodes.
#
# - W3C Organization Ontology, second use (same spec fetch as the
#   `org:Role` grounding above): `org:OrganizationalUnit` ("used to define
#   an organization in terms of the sub-units that it comprises") is the
#   correct fit for the account/subscription/project containment boundary
#   each of the three clouds imposes on every resource this pack's
#   capabilities create. Three INSTANCES only -- no new class -- are
#   declared: `urn:gymact:multicloud:containment:aws-account`,
#   `...azure-subscription`, `...gcp-project`, each multi-typed
#   `org:OrganizationalUnit, skos:Concept` and placed in a third new
#   `skos:ConceptScheme`, `urn:gymact:multicloud:scheme:resource-kind`
#   (a "ResourceKindScheme" classifying the kind of containment resource
#   each simulated identifier is generated under -- `_AWS_ACCOUNT_ID`,
#   `_AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID`, `_GCP_PROJECT_ID` in
#   `src/gymact/gyms/multicloud.py`), each with `skos:broader` into the
#   matching provider concept from the taxonomy above. `org:Membership`
#   is again deliberately not instantiated (same reasoning as the
#   `org:Role` grounding: no specific assignment *event* is being
#   catalogued here, only the resource-kind taxonomy itself).
#
# - DQV (Data Quality Vocabulary): evaluated and REJECTED for this pass.
#   `gymact.gyms.multicloud.MulticloudEnvironment.verify()` was read
#   directly (src/gymact/gyms/multicloud.py, `verify()` method): it does
#   `passed = all(observed.get(key) == value for key, value in
#   expected.items())` -- a plain dict-equality diff of a caller-supplied
#   `expected` mapping against the real observed state. That is a real
#   verification *decision* (state-based, per this repo's own testing
#   discipline) but it does not compute or expose any independent quality
#   *measurement* -- no freshness timestamp, no completeness ratio, no
#   score of any kind is produced or returned anywhere in this method or
#   provider. DQV's own model (`dqv:QualityMeasurement` = a `dqv:metric` +
#   a value) requires exactly that kind of measurement to attach to, which
#   this provider's real code does not produce. Per this task's own
#   instruction ("ONLY if multicloud.py's real verify() implementation
#   produces a real quality signal ... check first, do not add
#   speculatively"), DQV is NOT added anywhere in this file. If `verify()`
#   is later extended to compute e.g. a real staleness/completeness ratio,
#   DQV would become a real fit at that point, not before.
#
# - QUDT: evaluated and REJECTED. QUDT's actual purpose (fetched
#   https://qudt.org/schema/qudt/, already a declared `prof:isProfileOf`
#   member of `profile.ttl` for future dimensional-metric use) is typed
#   quantities with units (`qudt:QuantityValue`, `qudt:unit`,
#   `qudt:numericValue`). None of this pack's 20 capabilities carry any
#   quantity-with-unit fact: `instance_type`, `zone`, `bucket_name`,
#   `role_name`, `policy_arn`, `principal_id`, `role_definition`,
#   `account_name`, `vm_name`, `account_id`, `member`, `role` (the full set
#   of real payload keys read via `_require`/`payload.get` across every
#   `_aws_*`/`_azure_*`/`_gcp_*` handler in `src/gymact/gyms/multicloud.py`)
#   are all opaque identifier/name strings, never a measured quantity. No
#   QUDT term is added.
#
# - GeoSPARQL: evaluated and REJECTED. GeoSPARQL (fetched
#   https://www.ogc.org/standard/geosparql/) models geometry/location --
#   `geo:Feature`, `geo:Geometry`, WKT/GML literals. This pack's only
#   location-shaped payload value is `zone` (`gcp_compute_create_instance`,
#   e.g. `"us-central1-a"`) and the fixed `_AWS_REGION = "us-east-1"`
#   constant -- both are opaque cloud-provider region/zone identifier
#   strings with no real coordinate geometry or spatial-query use anywhere
#   in this provider's actual code (no bounding box, no distance
#   calculation, no WKT literal is ever constructed or compared). Modeling
#   a zone string as a `geo:Feature` would assert geometric semantics this
#   simulated provider does not actually compute over. No GeoSPARQL term is
#   added.
#
# - DPV (Data Privacy Vocabulary): evaluated and REJECTED. DPV (fetched
#   https://w3c.github.io/dpv/dpv/) models personal-data processing --
#   `dpv:PersonalData`, `dpv:ProcessingPurpose`, `dpv:LegalBasis`. This
#   pack's payloads never carry any personal data field of any kind: no
#   name, no email, no address, nothing PII-shaped appears in
#   `_require`/`payload.get` calls anywhere in
#   `src/gymact/gyms/multicloud.py` (identifiers are cloud-resource names
#   like `role_name`/`bucket_name`/`vm_name`, not person-identifying data).
#   `principal_id`/`member` (the closest candidates) are opaque IAM
#   principal/service-account identifiers, not personal data about a
#   natural person. No DPV term is added.
#
# - SPDX: evaluated and REJECTED. SPDX (fetched
#   https://spdx.github.io/spdx-spec/v2.3/) models software package
#   provenance and licensing -- `spdx:Package`, `spdx:File`,
#   `spdx:licenseDeclared`. This pack catalogs cloud-infrastructure API
#   capabilities (IAM roles, storage buckets, compute instances), not
#   software packages, files, or licenses of any kind -- there is no
#   package/file/license concept anywhere in this gym's real domain. No
#   SPDX term is added.
#
# - FOAF: evaluated and REJECTED. FOAF (fetched
#   http://xmlns.com/foaf/spec/) models named individual people and their
#   social/personal attributes -- `foaf:Person`, `foaf:name`,
#   `foaf:mbox`. This pack has no named-individual-person concept
#   anywhere: every identity-shaped resource it creates
#   (`aws.iam.create_role`, `gcp.iam.create_service_account`) is a
#   machine/service identity, already covered by `org:Role` (the AWS case)
#   or deliberately left ungrounded (the GCP case, per the existing
#   research-gap note above) -- neither is a `foaf:Person`. No FOAF term is
#   added.
#
# =============================================================================
# Third pass: security as a native fourth service-domain, not a bolt-on pack.
# A cloud gym that models IAM/storage/compute but has no way to represent a
# security-group/firewall rule is an incomplete cloud model; a caller should
# not be able to omit it by simply not depending on a separate pack. Adds one
# new `skos:Concept` (`service-domain:network-security`, a peer to the
# existing IAM/Storage/Compute concepts in the same
# `scheme:service-domain`) and six new `sosa:Procedure` capabilities, two per
# provider (one DO, one READ), bringing the total from 20 to 26.
#
# The three new DO capabilities (`aws.ec2.authorize_security_group_ingress`,
# `azure.network.create_security_rule`, `gcp.compute.insert_firewall`) reuse
# the identical `odrl:Permission` + `dct:temporal time:Interval`
# authority-window grounding already established above for the three IAM
# policy/role-assignment operations -- no new research pass was needed: a
# security-group/firewall ingress rule is the same authority-grant shape
# ("this permission holds starting now, for an interval") as an IAM policy
# attachment, so the existing rationale applies directly. The three new READ
# capabilities (`describe_security_groups`, `list_security_rules`,
# `list_firewalls`) follow the plain `sosa:Procedure, skos:Concept` shape
# with no extra typing, matching every existing `list_*`/`describe_*`
# capability in this file.

@prefix dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix sosa: <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/> .
@prefix odrl: <http://www.w3.org/ns/odrl/2/> .
@prefix org: <http://www.w3.org/ns/org#> .
@prefix dcat: <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix time: <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#> .

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SKOS taxonomy: provider, service-domain, and resource-kind (containment)
# concept schemes. Every capability below is additionally typed skos:Concept
# and linked skos:broader into exactly one provider concept and one
# service-domain concept, mirroring src/gymact/ontology/profile.ttl's own
# standing/roles/interaction skos:ConceptScheme pattern, generalized here to
# a taxonomy dimension this pack (not the core profile) owns.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

<urn:gymact:multicloud:scheme:provider>
    a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    dct:title "Multicloud gym: cloud provider taxonomy" .

<urn:gymact:multicloud:provider:aws>
    a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme <urn:gymact:multicloud:scheme:provider> ;
    skos:prefLabel "AWS" ;
    skos:definition "Amazon Web Services -- the provider namespace for every urn:gymact:multicloud:aws:capability:* node in this file." .

<urn:gymact:multicloud:provider:azure>
    a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme <urn:gymact:multicloud:scheme:provider> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Azure" ;
    skos:definition "Microsoft Azure -- the provider namespace for every urn:gymact:multicloud:azure:capability:* node in this file." .

<urn:gymact:multicloud:provider:gcp>
    a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme <urn:gymact:multicloud:scheme:provider> ;
    skos:prefLabel "GCP" ;
    skos:definition "Google Cloud Platform -- the provider namespace for every urn:gymact:multicloud:gcp:capability:* node in this file." .

<urn:gymact:multicloud:scheme:service-domain>
    a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    dct:title "Multicloud gym: service-domain taxonomy" .

<urn:gymact:multicloud:service-domain:iam>
    a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme <urn:gymact:multicloud:scheme:service-domain> ;
    skos:prefLabel "IAM" ;
    skos:definition "Identity and access management: role/service-account creation, policy attachment/binding, role assignment, and their list operations." .

<urn:gymact:multicloud:service-domain:storage>
    a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme <urn:gymact:multicloud:scheme:service-domain> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Storage" ;
    skos:definition "Object/blob storage container creation and listing (S3 buckets, Azure storage accounts, GCS buckets)." .

<urn:gymact:multicloud:service-domain:compute>
    a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme <urn:gymact:multicloud:scheme:service-domain> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Compute" ;
    skos:definition "Virtual machine / instance provisioning and listing (EC2, Azure VMs, GCE instances)." .

<urn:gymact:multicloud:service-domain:network-security>
    a skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme <urn:gymact:multicloud:scheme:service-domain> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Network Security" ;
    skos:definition "Security-group/firewall rule authorization, revocation, and listing -- the network-perimeter control surface every cloud account exposes alongside IAM, storage, and compute. A cloud gym that models IAM/storage/compute but has no way to represent a security-group/firewall rule is an incomplete cloud model; this is a native peer service-domain, not a bolt-on." .

<urn:gymact:multicloud:scheme:resource-kind>
    a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    dct:title "Multicloud gym: containment resource-kind taxonomy" .

<urn:gymact:multicloud:containment:aws-account>
    a org:OrganizationalUnit, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme <urn:gymact:multicloud:scheme:resource-kind> ;
    skos:broader <urn:gymact:multicloud:provider:aws> ;
    skos:prefLabel "AWS Account" ;
    skos:definition "The account-level org:OrganizationalUnit every ARN this provider generates is scoped under (the fixed, obviously-simulated _AWS_ACCOUNT_ID constant in src/gymact/gyms/multicloud.py)." .

<urn:gymact:multicloud:containment:azure-subscription>
    a org:OrganizationalUnit, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme <urn:gymact:multicloud:scheme:resource-kind> ;
    skos:broader <urn:gymact:multicloud:provider:azure> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Azure Subscription" ;
    skos:definition "The subscription-level org:OrganizationalUnit every Azure resource ID this provider generates is scoped under (_AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID, and the _AZURE_RESOURCE_GROUP nested within it, in src/gymact/gyms/multicloud.py)." .

<urn:gymact:multicloud:containment:gcp-project>
    a org:OrganizationalUnit, skos:Concept ;
    skos:inScheme <urn:gymact:multicloud:scheme:resource-kind> ;
    skos:broader <urn:gymact:multicloud:provider:gcp> ;
    skos:prefLabel "GCP Project" ;
    skos:definition "The project-level org:OrganizationalUnit every GCP resource name this provider generates is scoped under (_GCP_PROJECT_ID in src/gymact/gyms/multicloud.py)." .

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AWS (boto3-style operation names: iam.create_role, ec2.run_instances, ...)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

<urn:gymact:multicloud:aws:capability:iam.create_role>
    a sosa:Procedure, skos:Concept ;
    dct:title "aws.iam.create_role" ;
    dct:type <urn:gymact:consequence:do> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso org:Role ;
    skos:broader <urn:gymact:multicloud:provider:aws>, <urn:gymact:multicloud:service-domain:iam> .

<urn:gymact:multicloud:aws:capability:iam.attach_role_policy>
    a sosa:Procedure, odrl:Permission, skos:Concept ;
    dct:title "aws.iam.attach_role_policy" ;
    dct:type <urn:gymact:consequence:do> ;
    dct:temporal <urn:gymact:multicloud:aws:authority-window:iam.attach_role_policy> ;
    skos:broader <urn:gymact:multicloud:provider:aws>, <urn:gymact:multicloud:service-domain:iam> .

<urn:gymact:multicloud:aws:authority-window:iam.attach_role_policy>
    a time:Interval .

<urn:gymact:multicloud:aws:capability:iam.list_roles>
    a sosa:Procedure, skos:Concept ;
    dct:title "aws.iam.list_roles" ;
    dct:type <urn:gymact:consequence:read> ;
    skos:broader <urn:gymact:multicloud:provider:aws>, <urn:gymact:multicloud:service-domain:iam> .

<urn:gymact:multicloud:aws:capability:s3.create_bucket>
    a sosa:Procedure, skos:Concept ;
    dct:title "aws.s3.create_bucket" ;
    dct:type <urn:gymact:consequence:do> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso dcat:Distribution ;
    skos:broader <urn:gymact:multicloud:provider:aws>, <urn:gymact:multicloud:service-domain:storage> .

<urn:gymact:multicloud:aws:capability:s3.list_buckets>
    a sosa:Procedure, skos:Concept ;
    dct:title "aws.s3.list_buckets" ;
    dct:type <urn:gymact:consequence:read> ;
    skos:broader <urn:gymact:multicloud:provider:aws>, <urn:gymact:multicloud:service-domain:storage> .

<urn:gymact:multicloud:aws:capability:ec2.run_instances>
    a sosa:Procedure, skos:Concept ;
